 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "A thick-film element of noble metal in glass sits on a ceramic substrate between internal metal electrodes at each end, sealed under a second glass layer, laser trimmed to value and covered with an epoxy overcoat that carries the marking. The two end terminations are matte tin over a nickel barrier. In a jumper the resistive layer is a conductor."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Operating temperature",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "RC0402 to RC2512 operate from -55 °C to +155 °C; RC0075, RC0100 and RC0201 from -55 °C to +125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power rating and derating",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Rated power holds up to 70 °C ambient and falls linearly to zero at 155 °C (RC0402 to RC2512) or 125 °C (RC0075 to RC0201). Ratings at 70 °C: RC0075 1/50 W, RC0100 1/32 W, RC0201 1/20 W, RC0402 1/16 W or 1/8 W, RC0603 1/10 W or 1/5 W, RC0805 1/8 W or 1/4 W, RC1206 1/4 W or 1/2 W, RC1210 1/2 W, RC1218 1 W, RC2010 3/4 W, RC2512 1 W or 2 W. The higher grade is the double-power part, ordered with reel code 7W or 3W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Materials and moisture",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Thick-film parts with lead-free terminations; RoHS compliant and halogen free, with a halogen-free epoxy. Lead in the glass of the electrodes, resistive element and glass layers falls under a RoHS exemption. Moisture sensitivity level 1."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Reel label",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The internal 2D reel label carries \"LFP\" for lead-free process; a customised label may carry \"LFP\" or another symbol."
  }
 ],
